    {
      "id": "job-ingest-ci-failures",
      "name": "ingest-ci-failures",
      "prompt": "Check open PRs on ${HERMES_PROJECT_REPO:-owner/project} for:\n1. Merge conflicts (where `mergeable` is \"CONFLICTING\" or `mergeStateStatus` is \"DIRTY\")\n2. Failing CI checks (where any status check has failed)\n\nApply the following logic for each open PR (ignoring dependabot PRs where branches start with \"dependabot/\"):\n\n## Case A: Merge Conflicts\nIf a PR has merge conflicts:\n1. **Deduplication**: Check the Kanban board (via SQLite queries or `hermes kanban list`) to see if there is already an active (non-archived, non-done) card on the board containing \"Resolve merge conflicts in <branch>\" in its title or targeting `<branch>`.\n   - If an active card exists, skip it.\n2. **Card Creation**: If no active card exists, create a paired coder + reviewer task with workspace_kind=worktree. The fix should be pushed directly to the existing PR's branch (not a new branch).\n\n## Case B: CI Failures\nIf a PR has failing CI checks:\n1. **Deduplication**: Check if there's already an active kanban card for this PR's failure. If so, skip.\n2. **Re-trigger**: If the last successful run on this branch is more recent than the failed run, the failure is stale — skip.\n3. **Card Creation**: Create a `[FIX-<timestamp>]` card on the kanban board with workspace_kind=worktree.\n\nReport what was found: how many PRs scanned, how many conflicts, how many CI failures.",
      "skills": ["project-operations", "github-pr-workflow"],
      "model": "deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash",
      "provider": "openrouter",
      "script": "ingest-ci-failures.py",
      "no_agent": false,
      "schedule": {"kind": "interval", "minutes": 5, "display": "every 5m"},
      "schedule_display": "every 5m",
      "repeat": {"times": null, "completed": 0},
      "enabled": true,
      "deliver": "telegram",
      "workdir": "${HERMES_PROJECT_DIR:-/home/user/project}"
    },
    {
      "id": "job-ingest-deploy-failures",
      "name": "ingest-deploy-failures",
      "prompt": "A deploy pipeline just failed on ${HERMES_PROJECT_REPO:-owner/project}. The script above detected this is a NEW failure (not in state tracking). Apply dedup: (1) if there are open kanban fix cards on this branch → silent exit (fix in flight), (2) if there's an open PR on this branch → re-trigger CI, (3) neither → analyze the failure and create a fix card on the kanban board with workspace_kind=worktree.\n\nBRANCH NAMING: When creating fix cards, the branch name must be unique per task. Append the task ID to the branch name: fix/df-<timestamp>-<short-name>-<task-id>. This prevents git worktree collisions.\n\nCheck the deploy run at the JOB level (not workflow conclusion). A workflow can be 'failure' while Deploy to Staging is 'success' (non-gating test failed). Only create fix cards when the Deploy to Staging job itself failed.",
      "skills": ["project-operations", "github-pr-workflow"],
