      "id": "job-build-reviewer-resolve",
      "name": "build-reviewer-resolve",
      "prompt": "Check the ${HERMES_KANBAN_BOARD:-project-dev} kanban board for blocked code-reviewer cards that need auto-resolution.\n\n## Instructions\n1. Query the kanban board for tasks where status=blocked AND assignee=code-reviewer.\n2. For each blocked card, read the block reason and comments.\n3. If the block reason starts with \"review-failed:\" — this is a failed code review that needs auto-resolution. Load the kanban-orchestrator skill's Automated Review-Failed Resolution playbook and follow it exactly:\n   - Read the reviewer's structured comment (findings, files, verification)\n   - Extract the fix requirements\n   - Create a new coder card with the reviewer's findings baked into the body (include branch guardrails and BASE BRANCH from the original card)\n   - Create a paired code-reviewer card with parents=[new_coder_id]\n   - Comment on and archive the old blocked reviewer card\n4. If the block reason is something else — skip it and leave it for human triage.\n5. If a card has been resolved 3+ times already — escalate: do not create another fix card, instead comment asking for human review.\n\nReport what you did: how many blocked cards found, how many auto-resolved, what cards were created.",
